6. PRO TIPS
============================================================

TIP 1: COMMIT OFTEN

Small commits are easier to understand and manage than large commits containing many unrelated changes.

TIP 2: WRITE CLEAR COMMIT MESSAGES

Use meaningful commit messages.

Good examples:

    Fix login bug
    Add user authentication
    Update API integration
    Improve error handling

Avoid vague messages such as:

    updates
    changes
    done

TIP 3: USE .env FOR SECRETS

Never hardcode API keys, passwords, or other sensitive values in your Python source code.

Store them in environment variables and keep your actual .env file out of Git.

TIP 4: KEEP IT SIMPLE

Do not over-engineer small projects.

Start with a simple structure and introduce additional files, folders, and tools when the project actually needs them.

TIP 5: KEEP YOUR DEPENDENCIES ORGANIZED

Use uv add to manage project dependencies instead of manually installing packages without updating your project configuration.

TIP 6: COMMIT uv.lock

Include uv.lock in Git so that other developers can reproduce the same resolved dependency versions.

